<div class="form-wrap">

  <div class="rail" id="rail"></div>

  <div id="tbFormSteps">
  <!-- STEP 1: hat + colors -->
  <section class="tbstep active" data-step="1">
    <div class="tbstep-head"><div class="tbstep-num">1</div><h2>Choose your hat</h2><div class="tbstep-sum" id="sum1"></div></div>
    <div class="tbstep-body">
      <p class="tbstep-hint">Front embroidery is included on every hat. Pick a style, then choose your colors right below it.</p>
      <a href="#customerHats" class="ch-peek" id="chPeek" aria-label="See hats we've made for customers"></a>
      <div class="hat-filters" id="hatFilters"></div>
      <div class="hats" id="hats"></div>
      <a href="/pages/quote" class="quote-redirect">Don't see what you're looking for? <strong>Get a custom quote instead</strong></a>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="next" id="next1" disabled>Choose Quantity</button></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STEP 2: quantity -->
  <section class="tbstep" data-step="2">
    <div class="tbstep-head"><div class="tbstep-num">2</div><h2>How many?</h2><div class="tbstep-sum" id="sum2"></div></div>
    <div class="tbstep-body">
      <p class="tbstep-hint"><strong>5 hat minimum.</strong> Wholesale pricing starts at 10, with additional volume discounts at 24+. Mixed colors all count toward the same total.</p>
      <div class="qty-row">
        <div class="field"><label for="qty">Total quantity (5 minimum)</label><input class="qty-input" id="qty" type="number" min="5" step="1" inputmode="numeric" value="5"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="price-now" id="priceNow"></div>
      <div id="nudge"></div>
      <div id="splitHost"></div>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="back" data-back="1">Back</button><button type="button" class="next" id="next2" disabled>Add Your Design</button></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- STEP 3: design -->
  <section class="tbstep" data-step="3">
    <div class="tbstep-head"><div class="tbstep-num">3</div><h2>Your design</h2><div class="tbstep-sum" id="sum3"></div></div>
    <div class="tbstep-body">
      <p class="tbstep-hint">Send your logo in any format. We digitize it for embroidery free and email a mockup before we stitch.</p>

      <p class="fld">Decoration style <button type="button" class="info-btn" id="puffBtn">What is 3D puff?</button></p>
      <div class="chips" id="decos"></div>
      <div class="info-panel" id="puffInfo" hidden>
        <div class="info-compare">
          <div class="info-col"><div class="info-swatch flat-swatch">ABC</div><strong>Flat embroidery</strong><span>Stitched flush to the hat. Handles fine detail, small text, and intricate logos.</span></div>
          <div class="info-col"><div class="info-swatch puff-swatch">ABC</div><strong>3D puff</strong><span>Foam under the stitching lifts the design off the hat for a bold, raised look.</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="info-note">Puff works best with blocky letters and simple, bold shapes. It is not a fit for small text, thin lines, or fine detail, since the foam rounds those out. Not sure if your logo works? Leave it on flat and mention puff in the notes, and we will tell you honestly.</p>
        <p class="info-note"><strong>3D puff is front only.</strong> Any side or back embroidery will be stitched flat.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="fld">Placement</p>
      <div class="chips" id="places"></div>
      <div class="orient-note">
        <span class="orient-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9432;</span>
        <p><strong>Left and right are based on looking at the hat from the front, not the wearer's perspective.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div id="frontPosWrap">
        <p class="fld" style="font-size:13px">Front logo position</p>
        <div class="chips" id="frontPos"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">Front is included. <strong>Each additional location is $7 per hat.</strong> Both sides are $14 per hat. <strong>3D puff applies to the front logo only</strong>, so sides and back are always stitched flat.</p>

      <p class="fld">Your logo / artwork</p>
      <div class="uploads" id="uploads"></div>
      <p class="hint">One file per location: PNG, JPG, PDF, AI, or SVG, up to 10 MB each. Digitizing is free. No file handy? Skip it and email us after.</p>

      <a href="/pages/custom-patch-hats" class="patch-suggest">
        <div class="patch-suggest-body">
          <p class="patch-suggest-head">Very detailed logo?</p>
          <p>Fine lines, small text and intricate artwork lose detail in thread. A <strong>laser engraved leather patch</strong> holds detail far better and gives a premium look.</p>
          <span class="patch-suggest-cta">See patch hats &rarr;</span>
        </div>
      </a>

      <div class="embroidery-notice">
        <span class="en-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
        <div>
          <p class="en-ai-disclaimer"><strong>AI-generated artwork:</strong> AI images usually aren't ready to stitch as-is, so every one is reviewed by our design team before production. If yours needs to be professionally recreated into a production-ready file, we'll let you know and quote any recreation fee before anything is made. Standard digitizing is still free.</p>
          <div class="en-links">
            <button type="button" class="en-toggle" id="enToggle">View example</button>
            <button type="button" class="en-toggle" id="aiToggle">Using AI artwork? Read this</button>
          </div>
          <div class="en-ai" id="aiTips" hidden>
            <p><strong>Why AI art can be tricky to stitch</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li><b>Shading and gradients.</b> Thread is a solid color, so soft blends and glows can't be reproduced and come out as stripes or blotches.</li>
              <li><b>Too much detail.</b> Tiny textures, thin lines and busy backgrounds disappear at hat size.</li>
              <li><b>Messy lettering.</b> AI tools often warp letters or invent words. Small text needs to be clean and at least about 1/4 inch tall to read in thread.</li>
              <li><b>Fuzzy edges.</b> Most AI images are low resolution with blurry edges, so the shapes have to be redrawn before digitizing.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>Tips for an embroidery-friendly AI design</strong></p>
            <ul>
              <li>Ask for a <b>flat, simple logo</b> with <b>2 to 4 solid colors</b>, bold shapes and thick outlines.</li>
              <li>Say <b>no gradients, no shadows, no 3D effects</b>, on a plain or transparent background.</li>
              <li>Keep any text short and blocky, or add it in the notes and we'll set it in a clean font.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Send it either way. After review, we'll tell you if it needs recreating and quote any fee, then show you exactly how it will stitch in your free mockup before anything is made. Make sure you have the rights to use the design.</p>
